Why doesn't my model produce consistent responses?

The model's responses can sometimes appear inconsistent when given identical prompts. This is because the model is stochastic, meaning that different parts of its weights are unpredictably sampled every time it generates an output (this is called weight sampling). Upon serialization, the weights are congealed, effectively freezing them at the time of serialization. If the model is then trained or used to generate outputs, the observed discrepancies can be partially explained by the inherent variability of the weight sampling that occurred during serialization.

