Differences between GPU and CPU 

1. Structure 
CPU: 
- consisting of 4-64 homogeneous cores.
- cache size of up to 256KB data cache per CPU core.
- architected for low twin-thread latency.
- data bandwidth of approximately 10-20 GB/s.

GPU: 
- consisting of 1000s of homogeneous cores.
- cache size of up to 32KB data cache per GPU core.
- high data throughput over thousands of threads.
- data bandwidth of approximately 100s of GB/s.

2. Focus on the feature:
CPU:
- Latency ( APU ) such as "Control System"
- More FLOPS per clock through deeper design space.
- Optimized for sequential task execution.

GPU: 
- Bandwidth ( FLOPS )
- Optimized for parallel task execution 


