 Residual connections are a type of shortcut connection that allows information to bypass certain layers in a neural network. This can help prevent the problem of vanishing gradients, where the gradients of the loss function become too small to effectively train the model. In the context of transformers, residual connections are used to connect the input and output of each sub-layer, allowing the model to learn more complex relationships between the input and output. This can improve the performance of the transformer on tasks such as machine translation and text classification.
