2. The computational procedure in the authors’ experiments (DiagClass) successfully analyzes the output of individual self-attention heads & confirms that the heads’ specializations correspond to natural language features (which specifies the function of the given head).
3. Experiments suggest a (deterministic) relationship between changes in learned language features (in self-attention heads) & changes in the model’s predictions (in the textual-entailment dataset).
4. Head specialized in attending syntactic dependencies & head attending semantic relations (negation, singular/plural agreement, etc. ) always focus on “exact words" & “local regions.”

